id:                     E381
trigger_tool: powershell|git|device-controller
phase: prewrite|allocation
error_signature: HEAD/tree drift|allocation.*tree.*stale|controller.*tree.*drift
severity: 3
category:               device-control, snapshot-binding, successor-generation
match_keywords: staged tree, wrapper, controller, allocation record, authority, git write-tree, zero SSH
title: Bind wrapper and controller tree constants to the same final authority
root_cause: A successor freeze can bind the new staged tree while a mechanically copied outer wrapper or inner controller still emits the predecessor tree into the allocation object.
affected_scope: One-shot device controllers whose wrapper constructs allocation authority separately from the controller's local HEAD/tree prewrite gate.
verification_cmd: Generate a synthetic exact allocation from the real wrapper, run the production controller in offline mode, and require wrapper allocation tree, controller tree, authority tree and live git write-tree to be byte-identical.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: four-way-snapshot-binding
rec_description: Derive or assert every wrapper/controller snapshot constant against one final authority before claim, evidence creation, SSH or transfer.
rec_command: Fail the local matrix when any of wrapper allocation, controller constant, authority or git write-tree differs; bind the verified controller and wrapper hashes into final W4.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: production-offline-transaction-snapshot-projection
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach:
fallback_description:
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern: retry.*same.*run|ignore.*HEAD/tree drift|edit.*allocation.*after claim
forbid_1_reason: A consumed one-shot claim cannot be repaired by retrying or mutating its evidence after the fact.
forbid_1_consequence: Snapshot evidence may no longer describe the code sent to the device.
principles:
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
